EF AI Workspace (#186): the welcome screen greets the employee by first name; the chat direction setting no longer
flips the Arabic composer. Owner decision 2026-10-24: option B («اعتمد ب ونفذه»), no starter cards.

- Greeting (Chat/efGreeting.ts, Landing.tsx): «صباح الخير، نورة» from 04:00 and «مساء الخير، نورة» from 12:00 on the
  employee's device (English: morning, afternoon from 12:00, evening from 17:00); it changes at the boundary and is
  rechecked when the tab returns. The first word of the account name, compound first names kept whole («عبد الله»,
  «أبو بكر», Abdul Rahman); no name, or an email address, greets without one. The configured `customWelcome` (with its
  {{user.name}}) follows as the second line, or «كيف أساعدك اليوم؟» when none is set. Temporary chats and agent or
  model-spec landings are unchanged. Upstream's scheduled greetings are no longer shown (customWelcome replaced them).
- Composer direction (Chat/Input/composerDirection.ts, ChatForm.tsx, Files/FileFormChat.tsx): upstream reverses the
  composer's rows when Settings → Chat direction is right to left, assuming a left-to-right page. On an Arabic page the
  rows already run right to left, so Send moved to the start side and + to the end. The setting now reverses the rows
  on left-to-right pages only.

